// REQUIRES: host-linux-amd64 || host-linux-arm64
// RUN: rm -rf %t.d
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/runner-check.py --work %t.d/split %S/Inputs/runner --names nonl,interleave,bigout
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/runner-check.py --work %t.d/merged --merge %S/Inputs/runner --names nonl,interleave,bigout
// P04.19 (D4.14): output is the same bytes as from a binary: no newline at the
// end, megabytes of it, and standard output and error written in turn. The
// second run puts both streams in one file (`merge_output`, a binary's
// `2>&1`): the bytes then come in the order they were written.
